<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="Occiderunt" pubkey="" timestamp="1795633869" url="https://occiderunt.github.io/f-droid/repo" version="20002"><description>Android releases of Occiderunt apps, built and signed by Occiderunt. Bling is peer-to-peer chat with no server in the middle; Poirot is a pantry ledger.</description></repo><application id="org.vellum.bling"><id>org.vellum.bling</id><added>2026-11-23</added><lastupdated>2026-11-23</lastupdated><name>Bling</name><summary>Peer-to-peer chat with no server in the middle</summary><desc>Bling is a chat app that connects directly to the other people you are
talking to. There is no account, no sign-up and no relay server: messages
travel over a libp2p swarm between the devices themselves.

How it works:

* Your identity is a key pair generated on the device and stored locally.
* Peers find each other on the local network, or you paste an invite address
  to connect across networks.
* Each room is a gossipsub topic, so everyone in the room sees the same
  messages.

Things worth knowing:

* Rooms are open to anyone who knows the room name.
* History is kept on the device only, and the last 300 messages per room are
  kept.
* On Android 17 and later, the app asks for local network access so it can
  reach peers on your Wi-Fi.
* Notifications only appear when the app is in the background.
* Nothing is stored on a server, because there is no server.

Bling is free software under the MIT license.
</desc><license>MIT</license><categories>Internet,Communication</categories><category>Internet</category><web>https://occiderunt.github.io/bling/</web><source>https://github.com/occiderunt/bling</source><tracker>https://github.com/occiderunt/bling/issues</tracker><changelog>https://github.com/occiderunt/bling/releases</changelog><author>Occiderunt</author><marketversion></marketversion><marketvercode>1003000</marketvercode><package><version>1.3.0</version><versioncode>1003000</versioncode><apkname>org.vellum.bling_1003000.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">0d0bdf3891939cad0219fb1e246d499a32d12fa3c6b40be05ce42e6ecc86b92e</hash><size>12092247</size><sdkver>24</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-23</added><sig>b77c23ca666ca0595f09df402ca06f6d</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE,CAMERA,INTERNET,POST_NOTIFICATIONS,RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED,VIBRATE,WAKE_LOCK,org.vellum.bling.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><nativecode>arm64-v8a</nativecode></package><package><version>1.2.0</version><versioncode>1002000</versioncode><apkname>org.vellum.bling_1002000.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">654b944bd540f50ce1315313472cc8e229b0db49f5806c0cd16ba7de877bed9d</hash><size>12075863</size><sdkver>24</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-23</added><sig>b77c23ca666ca0595f09df402ca06f6d</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE,CAMERA,INTERNET,POST_NOTIFICATIONS,RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED,VIBRATE,WAKE_LOCK,org.vellum.bling.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><nativecode>arm64-v8a</nativecode></package><package><version>1.1.0</version><versioncode>1001000</versioncode><apkname>org.vellum.bling_1001000.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">35b1cd1653f516404fc1d9e683b6cb69f01975dc753c0b50205b2c6c1a764b39</hash><size>11220644</size><sdkver>24</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-23</added><sig>b77c23ca666ca0595f09df402ca06f6d</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,INTERNET,POST_NOTIFICATIONS,RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED,WAKE_LOCK,org.vellum.bling.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><nativecode>arm64-v8a</nativecode></package><package><version>1.0.1</version><versioncode>1000001</versioncode><apkname>org.vellum.bling_1000001.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">14e5f2d9fb4c23c820b71a841a88252c89bea58bf6791de54c5cce08d9b53b47</hash><size>11279061</size><sdkver>24</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-23</added><sig>b77c23ca666ca0595f09df402ca06f6d</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,INTERNET,POST_NOTIFICATIONS,RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED,WAKE_LOCK,org.vellum.bling.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><nativecode>arm64-v8a</nativecode></package></application><application id="org.vellum.netstudysynopsis"><id>org.vellum.netstudysynopsis</id><added>2026-11-23</added><lastupdated>2026-11-23</lastupdated><name>NET Study Synopsis</name><summary>The four Gospels side by side, one screen at a time</summary><desc>A synopsis of the four Gospels for reading and study. Rather than
blending the accounts into one harmony, it keeps each Evangelist in
his own column, in his own order, over the standard pericope
sequence.

On a phone the columns become a swipeable strip: one Gospel fills the
screen, the tabs above jump between Matthew, Mark, Luke and John, and
the outline lives in a drawer behind the menu button. Tapping a verse
pins it and opens its closest wording in the other Gospels; tapping a
parallel jumps to that Gospel at the matching verse.

Passage text is the NET Bible, fetched from the NET Bible API and
cached on the device for offline reading. Scripture quotations are
copyright Biblical Studies Press, L.L.C., and are used by permission.

The app is free software under the GNU GPL v3.
</desc><license>GPL-3.0-only</license><categories>Reading</categories><category>Reading</category><web>https://net-study.github.io/netstudy-synopsis/</web><source>https://github.com/NET-Study/netstudy-synopsis</source><tracker>https://github.com/NET-Study/netstudy-synopsis/issues</tracker><changelog>https://github.com/NET-Study/netstudy-synopsis/releases</changelog><author>NET Study</author><marketversion></marketversion><marketvercode>1001002</marketvercode><package><version>1.1.2</version><versioncode>1001002</versioncode><apkname>org.vellum.netstudysynopsis_1001002.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">3fd613aacfbaa2a15041e79b54efb02df670feece1281f6a482273169b9db6c1</hash><size>7543761</size><sdkver>24</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-23</added><sig>6d28c368ece522ddef05e4cbcb6683b7</sig><permissions>INTERNET,org.vellum.netstudysynopsis.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><nativecode>arm64-v8a</nativecode></package></application><application id="org.vellum.poirot"><id>org.vellum.poirot</id><added>2026-11-24</added><lastupdated>2026-11-25</lastupdated><name>Poirot</name><summary>A pantry ledger for what is on your shelves</summary><desc>Poirot keeps track of what is in your pantry: how much is left, when it
needs using, and which shelf it lives on.

Shelves are yours to name and recolour: Left Pantry, Fridge, Freezer,
Spice Rack, or anything else. Items carry a quantity with a sensible
unit, an optional expiry date and an optional low-stock threshold. The
home screen surfaces anything expiring soon, running low or already out,
and one searchable list holds every item with filters for the same.

A JSON backup copies the whole pantry to a file and restores it on
another device.

Everything stays on the device. No account, no network, no sync.
Poirot is free software under the MIT license.
